# NovelGuard Web UI

UI lives under `web/`. Canonical tokens and UX: [DESIGN.md](mdc:DESIGN.md).
Generic Tailwind guidance belongs in official docs, not this rule.

## Rules

1. Define colors, spacing, type, and radius in `web/src/styles/globals.css` `@theme` from DESIGN.md.
2. Avoid ad-hoc hex values in components.
3. Use semantic classes such as `bg-surface`, `text-on-surface`, `text-primary`, and `rounded-md`.
4. Token changes start in DESIGN.md, then `globals.css`; keep both in the same PR.
5. Destructive flows require dry-run preview, user approval, then apply.
6. Tailwind classes belong in `web/**`, not Python `src/` except static assets.
7. Product default is dark; add light overrides only when both themes ship.
8. Extract repeated class lists into `web/src/components/` when reuse is meaningful.
9. Prefer `@theme` tokens over arbitrary values.

## File Map

| Concern | Path |
| ------- | ---- |
| Design system | [DESIGN.md](mdc:DESIGN.md) |
| Theme CSS | `web/src/styles/globals.css` |
| Primitives | `web/src/components/ui/` |
